docs {
  # Delegation requests: draft lookup and counts

  BDD scenarios for three enduser endpoints under `/accessmanagement/api/v1/enduser/request`:

  - `GET draft`: the draft a service owner prepared for the user, before the user
    confirms and sends it.
  - `GET sent/count`: how many requests a party has sent.
  - `GET received/count`: how many requests a party has received.

  Each subfolder is one scenario, with steps named `NN_GIVEN|WHEN|THEN|AND|CLEANUP_...`
  and ordered by `seq`. Every scenario starts by having the service owner create a draft
  package request through
  `POST /accessmanagement/api/v1/serviceowner/delegationrequests/package`. The create is
  idempotent for drafts (an open draft for the same parties and package is returned
  instead of a new one), and every scenario ends by withdrawing the draft, so the folder
  can run repeatedly. Requests cannot be deleted, so every run leaves one withdrawn
  request behind; the assertions never depend on the absolute number of requests.

  ## Personas and fixtures

  Seed data comes from the `draftAndCounts` section of
  `testdata/delegationrequest-scenarios/<env>.js`, which picks the personas from the
  existing testdata files instead of copying their ids:

  - requester: a private person the service owner asks access for.
  - organization: the organization the access is asked at, acting through its daglig
    leder.
  - outsider: a private person with no relation to either.
  - The service owner is ttd, with the `altinn:serviceowner/delegationrequests.write`
    scope.

  Every step mints its own token through `helpers.js` (`loginAs(persona, scopes?)` and
  `loginAsServiceOwner()`).

  ## Environments

  Runs against AT22. The request endpoints sit behind the feature flags
  `AccessMgmt.Controller.RequestAssignment.Resource` and
  `AccessMgmt.Controller.RequestAssignment.Package`; with both off every endpoint here
  returns 404.
}
